    <!-- ==================================================================
         INSPIRE HAND SELF-CONTACT — every pair WITHIN one hand, disabled.

         An Inspire hand is a self-contained gripper with its own firmware and
         its own joint limits; MoveIt plans the ARM and drives the hand through
         named states (grasp, half_grasp, release, open_tenth). A closing hand
         puts its fingers against its own palm and against each other — that is
         what a gripper does, not a collision to plan around. Leaving them
         checked makes the `hand_grasp` stage unsolvable: measured, the left
         hand's `grasp` state reports ILH_left_index_1 vs ILH_plam.

         STATED COMPLETELY, ON PURPOSE. The pre-2026-08-17 SRDF disabled 884 of
         the 930 possible same-hand pairs and the regenerated matrix disabled
         667 — in both cases whichever ones a random sampler happened to find.
         Which 884 was an accident of sampling, not a decision. All 930 are
         listed here so the rule is the rule, and a re-run of collisions_updater
         cannot quietly change it.

         SCOPE, and it is narrow: WITHIN one hand only. Left hand vs right hand
         (ILH vs IRH) stays fully enabled, as does hand vs arm, hand vs cover,
         hand vs lever and hand vs glove unit — see the policy note above.
         ================================================================== -->
    <disable_collisions link1="ILH_base_link" link2="ILH_left_index_1" reason="Gripper self-contact by design"/>
    <disable_collisions link1="ILH_base_link" link2="ILH_left_index_2" reason="Gripper self-contact by design"/>
